index 89bde294..977b39b7 100644
--- a/skill-guides/orca-cli/references/browser.md
+++ b/skill-guides/orca-cli/references/browser.md
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@ Browser rules:
 Common recoveries:
 
 - `browser_no_tab`: open a tab with `ORCA tab create --url <url> --json`.
+- When a Core Chromium page needs a person to sign in, ask them to use **Take control** in that browser tab and **Return control** when finished. If a command returns `browser_page_manually_controlled`, use `ORCA tab control-status --page <browserPageId> --json` to check for `result.state: "available"`. Then run `ORCA snapshot --page <browserPageId> --json` and choose your next action from the page as it stands.
 - `browser_stale_ref`: run `ORCA snapshot --page <browserPageId> --json` and retry on the same page with fresh refs.
 - `browser_element_not_interactable`: the element can't take that command, and the message says why (not a text field, disabled, read-only, not a `<select>`, opened no file picker). Re-snapshot and pick the right ref; for a custom dropdown, click it and then click the option.
 - `browser_tab_not_found`: run `ORCA tab list --json` before switching or closing.
